# Cloudflare Pages redirects (spec 0009).
#
# THE ROOT ADDRESS. The line below is the ONLY place that decides what `/` does. To give the main address to another product,
# change or replace this one line (or put a page or a function at `/`). Nothing under /dhiinterviews treats `/` as its home, so
# nothing else moves. Keep it a temporary (302) redirect, and note that Pages keeps the query string (`/?ref=ABC123` arrives intact;
# `pnpm verify:pages` checks it).
/ /dhiinterviews/landing 302

# The funnel's own short addresses (these stay whatever the root becomes).
/dhiinterviews /dhiinterviews/landing 302
/dhiinterviews/ /dhiinterviews/landing 302

# The private report link (spec 0010). Every /s/<code> address gets the same static page, with status 200 (a rewrite, so the address stays
# as it is). The page holds no student data; js/shared-boot.js reads the code from the address and fetches the report.
/s/* /dhiinterviews/shared 200
